@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+# Composition v1 — Artifact 001
+
+Status: offline synthetic engineering proof, not a historical reconstruction,
+artist-approved layout, published release, deployed interface, or merged change.
+Implementation remains inside the Portvs incubator. Final promotion owner remains
+unresolved; existing Media Ark, art-runtime, portfolio and exhibit apertures are
+unchanged.
+
+## One rendering backend, two authoring frontends
+
+The existing `render_triptych.py` is extended, not replaced. Its legacy CLI and
+manifest scheduler continue to create `Panel` / `Segment` objects. The new
+`composition.py` adapts versioned independent-loop state into the **same** objects,
+`render_segment`, encoding, temporary-file lifecycle and concatenation functions.
+Legacy canon scheduling remains a compatibility frontend; it is not falsely
+represented as independent-loop timing. The new state format does not serialize
+the legacy round scheduler or its audio/effect settings. Those remain reproducible
+through the original manifest/CLI. No second FFmpeg renderer was introduced.
+
+`export_project.py` is unchanged. Its renderer command builder was inspected;
+full generated-site/browser integration is not claimed by this proof.
+
+## State and exact clock semantics
+
+Schema: `portvs.composition/1`.
+Engine contract: `portvs-segments/1.0.0`.
+Selection algorithm: `sha256-loop-counter/1`.
+
+Time is a nonnegative **output-frame index** at the state's integer FPS. A source
+has a stable ID, relative path, SHA256, video/still kind and explicit rational
+logical duration. Hash validation and ffprobe validation precede rendering.
+A still's duration is a declared hold/loop interval, not an inferred file duration.
+All supplied synthetic videos have a two-second cycle and 48 source frames/sec;
+the eight compositions have 96 output frames at 24 frames/sec.
+
+Each stable loop identity has an ordered source bank, initial binding or seeded
+choice, reroll counter, rational offset, rational positive rate, rational trim
+window and held flag. Phases use Python `Fraction`, not accumulated float time.
+Sampling is deterministic at output frames; the media decoder samples the source
+at the compiled timestamp. Pixel/encoding equivalence across FFmpeg versions,
+codecs, thread counts or hardware is not promised.
+
+Events apply **before** sampling their frame. Array order resolves equal-frame
+operations. Every event and the complete initial state is retained for replay.
+
+| Operation | Defined effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `hold(value=true)` | Freeze only the target loop's source phase. No other clock resets. |
+| `hold(value=false)` | Resume from that phase, without catching up for held time. |
+| `reroll` | Increment only the target counter, choose from its ordered bank while excluding its previous source when another candidate exists, reset its phase to zero; preserve its held/rate state. This explicit action can change a held image. |
+| `swap` | Exchange two current source bindings only. IDs, banks, local phases, rates, trim windows and held states stay attached to their loops. Fail if a exchanged source cannot fit its destination trim. |
+| `move` | Replace one normalized rectangle in one named orientation. Do not change clocks, bindings or the other orientation. |
+
+Selection hashes compact UTF-8 JSON `[algorithm, seed, loop_id, counter]` with
+SHA256, interprets the digest as an unsigned big-endian integer and takes modulo
+the eligible bank length. No mutable global PRNG and no loop-evaluation-order
+dependency exist. This is reproducible selection, not a claim of cryptographic
+uniformity after modulo reduction. Source reuse is rejected unless explicitly
+enabled; a reroll that would violate that constraint fails validation rather than
+silently cloning a video into another aperture.
+
+## Presentation is separate from time
+
+Each state contains authored `portrait` and `landscape` layouts. Both map every
+active loop ID exactly once. Placement array order is explicit compositing order.
+Rectangles are normalized, fit is `cover` or `contain`, and cover crop focal points
+are normalized. Contain uses centered letterboxing. V1 rejects empty, overlapping,
+unknown or missing apertures instead of dropping/occluding loops.
+
+`orientation_for(width, height)` selects by actual dimensions (square selects
+portrait). It does not modify temporal state. Raster export bounds are rounded to
+even shared edges for YUV420 and reject a too-small target. Export dimensions must
+be even. No live-browser resize/rotation adapter was built or browser-tested.
+
+Counts 3, 4, 5 and 6 each have distinct authored paired maps in
+`make_artifact_001.py`. There is no generic grid fallback. The schema ceiling of
+16 loops is a defensive validation limit, **not** a tested performance claim for
+7–16 loops. No automatic perceptual/layout approval is implied.
+
+## Audio and deferred capabilities
+
+Legacy `none`, `panel` and `mix` modes, selected-panel semantics, gain/fades,
+forward/reverse/pingpong and tone options retain their existing implementation.
+New composition-v1 exports are silent. `audio: {mode: none, generative: null}` and
+`routing: []` reserve extension points; requesting active routing or generative
+sound fails explicitly. Arbitrary blend, masks, nesting, animation interpolation,
+negative rates, realtime playback, browser controls, spatial rendering and
+installation targets are not implemented in this tranche.
+
+## Reproduce the supplied proof
+
+Runtime: Python standard library, FFmpeg and ffprobe with libx264 support.
+The decoded-frame verification script additionally uses NumPy and Pillow;
+versions used are in `requirements-verification.txt`. No API keys/network or Mac
+software are required for the supplied synthetic inputs.
+
+From this incubator directory in the reproduction bundle:
+
+```sh
+python -m unittest -v test_composition
+python make_artifact_001.py --render-only --only 3
+python make_artifact_001.py --render-only --only 4
+python make_artifact_001.py --render-only --only 5
+python make_artifact_001.py --render-only --only 6
+python verify_artifact_001.py
+```
+
+`--render-only` uses the **supplied source bytes, state and hashes**, rather than
+regenerating inputs. `--resume` may reuse a video only when its state/code recipe,
+output hash, dimensions and frame count match. The final verifier remains a
+separate mandatory check; a container batch timeout is not a passed batch.
+
+One direct render command:
+
+```sh
+python render_triptych.py \
+  --composition work/artifact-001/state-4.json \
+  --orientation landscape --width 1920 --height 1080 \
+  --preset veryfast --crf 20 \
+  --output work/artifact-001/renders/4-landscape.mp4
+```
+
+`python make_artifact_001.py --prepare-only` regenerates the synthetic source banks
+and state fixtures. This changes source hashes if another encoder/toolchain emits
+different bytes; preserve the supplied source manifest for an exact source replay.
+`baseline_run.py` is the pre-refactor baseline command, intentionally guarded by
+the upstream renderer blob hash; it is not a post-refactor replay command.
+
+## Evidence actually obtained
+
+The upstream renderer blob was matched exactly to Git object
+`6155fa1b8c9d5284c3deda0eaf56b342e47cf1bc` from upstream commit
+`48da3da293ecd7604b6c9d3ce19d0bf49a70013d` before it was changed.
+Four unchanged baseline exports were rendered before refactoring and the three
+full-height columns were visually inspected.
+
+37 tests pass, including 1,296 legacy schedule/FFmpeg-command comparisons, plus a
+separate silent-source/nondefault-gain comparison. Four actual post-refactor
+legacy outputs match baseline bytes under the same toolchain and CPU affinity.
+This is not 1,296 independently encoded render tests or a whole-repository CI run.
+No pre-existing renderer unit-test suite was retrieved in the scoped searches;
+the new regression suite and existing CLI were used. The unrelated generated-site
+verifiers were not run.
+
+Eight actual full-HD, four-second moving videos plus a one-second still/video
+adapter render exist. Each full-HD video is decoded for all 96 frames. Checks
+verify panel presence throughout, movement of every loop, and held-phase visual
+stability. A first-render freeze bug (black frames after the first held frame) was
+caught by this check, repaired with an explicit one-frame loop, and the complete
+family was rerendered. The passing results describe the corrected files only.
+Reference frames were visually inspected separately. Inspection-sheet labels are
+outside the artwork; MP4s and extracted artwork PNGs contain no interface chrome.
+
+Generated states, input/output hashes, source bytes, ffprobe facts, commands,
+verification results and baseline receipts live under ignored `work/` in the
+reproduction bundle. No private historical source media is included.
